        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garberville%2C_California"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town sits on the South Fork of the Eel River, 52 miles south‑southeast of Eureka, at an elevation of 535 feet.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garberville%2C_California"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Garberville is the main town of the Mateel Region, covering parts of the Mattole and Eel River watersheds.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garberville%2C_California"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1853, Spanish explorer Antone Garcia settled near Town Gulch, which now runs through Garberville.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
